From a0af9dd1e5e5d8f7dd642cf8513ec2edcd23e749 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:18:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] nvk/rm: build glue, RM API subset and librmclient loader

Add -Dnvk-rm (feature, default disabled) for an nvkmd backend that drives
the GPU through the NVIDIA Resource Manager of the open kernel modules
(open-gpu-kernel-modules), using librmclient (Conduit, guest/rmclient,
MIT) for the /dev/nvidiactl escape interface, or a forwarded equivalent
in a VM.

librmclient is dlopen()ed at runtime (librmclient.so.0, librmclient.so,
or $NVK_RMCLIENT_LIB), so building only needs its header.  If pkg-config
does not find "rmclient", a verbatim copy of librmclient's rmclient.h is
used.  Entry points beyond the base contract (crm_map_dma2,
crm_free_quiet, crm_event_open/close/drain) are looked up and used when
present.

nvrm/nvrm_api.h carries the minimal subset of NVIDIA's RM API this backend
uses (classes, alloc parameters, controls, host methods), copied from
open-gpu-kernel-modules 610.57.04 (MIT), with static asserts on the
parameter sizes RM expects.

